{"content":[{"c":["AHIMELECH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. A priest at Nob who aided David in his flight from Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.21.1-9","r":"1Sam.21.1-9","rawR":"1Sam.21.1-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.21.1-9","value":"1Sam.21.1-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 21:1-9"},"). When he was asked for food, all he could provide was the holy bread in the tabernacle (Jesus referred to this incident in ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.12.1-8","r":"Matt.12.1-8","rawR":"Matt.12.1-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.12.1-8","value":"Matt.12.1-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 12:1-8"},"). Doeg the Edomite subsequently reported this action to Saul, who ordered Ahimelech put to death. Saul’s guards were unwilling to execute a priest, but the informer Doeg had no such inhibitions. He killed Ahimelech and 84 other priests, plus their families and livestock (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.22.9-19","r":"1Sam.22.9-19","rawR":"1Sam.22.9-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.22.9-19","value":"1Sam.22.9-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 22:9-19"},"). Only Abiathar, Ahimelech’s son, escaped and fled to David’s protection (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.22.20-23","r":"1Sam.22.20-23","rawR":"1Sam.22.20-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.22.20-23","value":"1Sam.22.20-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:20-23"},"). ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.52.1-9","r":"Ps.52.1-9","rawR":"Ps.52.1-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.52.1-9","value":"Ps.52.1-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 52"}," was written by David as an indictment of Doeg’s treachery."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Hittite who joined David’s guerrilla force during his flight from Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.26.6","r":"1Sam.26.6","rawR":"1Sam.26.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.26.6","value":"1Sam.26.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 26:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Son of Abiathar and grandson of #1 above. This Ahimelech aided his father in the priesthood under King David (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.8.17","r":"2Sam.8.17","rawR":"2Sam.8.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.8.17","value":"2Sam.8.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 8:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.3,5,31","r":"1Chr.24.3,5,31","rawR":"1Chr.24.3,5,31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.3,5,31","value":"1Chr.24.3,5,31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 24:3, 5, 31"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.18.16","r":"1Chr.18.16","rawR":"1Chr.18.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.18.16","value":"1Chr.18.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 18:16"},", where some versions have Abimelech instead)."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Ahimelech","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 21:1-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.21.1-9","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.21.1-9","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.21.1-9"},{"anchorText":"Mt 12:1-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.12.1-8","rawQueryValue":"Matt.12.1-8","sourceRefExact":"Matt.12.1-8"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 22:9-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.22.9-19","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.22.9-19","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.22.9-19"},{"anchorText":"22:20-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.22.20-23","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.22.20-23","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.22.20-23"},{"anchorText":"Psalm 52","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.52.1-9","rawQueryValue":"Ps.52.1-9","sourceRefExact":"Ps.52.1-9"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 26:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.26.6","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.26.6","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.26.6"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 8:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.8.17","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.8.17","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.8.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 24:3, 5, 31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.24.3,5,31","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.24.3,5,31","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.24.3,5,31"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 18:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.18.16","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.18.16","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.18.16"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a8974cd6039628fd63a2751dd202dd0c33c1c94b14e3498271757014e8ea0560","sourceItemName":"Ahimelech","sourceItemOrder":190,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ahimelech","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ahimelech","title":"Ahimelech","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}